From 0edda0acc5c7ab8c883ba617ef0173686d134ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 08:13:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove filled Reputation Manager cards; fix cramped section
 spacing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reputation Manager (rep-findings-panel.tsx) still had the old filled
"no-ambient-glow surface-glass-1" card treatment on every panel — the
toolbar, the run-a-check bar, the timeline feed, and the detail panel —
plus its page had no bg-dot-grid wrapper at all, unlike every other
skill page. All four now match the established transparent+border
system, and the page shows the dot grid through.

Funnel Audit's Executive Report (simple-markdown.tsx) read as one
undifferentiated wall of text — a metric's last bullet and the next
major section's heading ("Recommendation Cards", "Data Gaps") sat only
16px apart with nothing to mark the boundary. Level-1 headings now get
a top divider and real vertical room so a section change is
unambiguous; list items and paragraphs got a bit more breathing room
too.

deliverables-panel.tsx ("Show Rate Setup"): bumped the main container's
padding and the tightest space-y-1 groupings (hooks, script beats,
recording checklists, page-audit lists) up a notch — same fix pattern.

Also: Leak Map's view-switcher toggle was labeled "Calendar" for what
is actually its verdict/report overview, not a calendar grid — added a
label/icon override to ViewSwitcher (view-switcher.tsx) so this mode
reads as "Overview" here while every view that's a real calendar keeps
the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
